wifi: mac80211: do not assign a chanctx to an AP_VLAN on hw restart

ieee80211_restart_hw() -> ieee80211_reconfig() walks every running
interface and calls ieee80211_assign_chanctx() for each active link
before it filters on interface type. The type switch that follows does
have a "nothing to do" case for NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN, but by then the
chanctx assignment has already been handed to the driver.

An AP_VLAN is deliberately never passed to the driver: every
drv_add_interface() call site in ieee80211_reconfig() skips that type, so
IEEE80211_SDATA_IN_DRIVER is never set on it. Its link chanctx_conf is
only a copy of the parent AP link's pointer, made when the VLAN is
opened, which means the pointer is non-NULL and the assignment is not
skipped by the "if (conf)" test either.

The result is that drv_assign_vif_chanctx() is reached with an sdata the
driver has never seen, check_sdata_in_driver() fires and the assignment
returns -EIO:

  WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 144 at drv_assign_vif_chanctx+0x120/0x13c
  wlanX.staN: Failed check-sdata-in-driver check, flags: 0x1
  Call trace:
   drv_assign_vif_chanctx
   ieee80211_reconfig
   ieee80211_restart_hw

Seen on a driver that restarts the hardware from a firmware health check
while a 4addr WDS client is associated, which is what creates the
AP_VLAN. Drivers that never restart the hardware with an AP_VLAN up do
not reach it, which is why it is rarely observed.

Skip the driver call for AP_VLAN so the driver is only given interfaces
it actually knows about. The parent AP link still gets its chanctx
assigned by its own pass through the same loop, so no configuration is
lost.

Index: backports-6.12.6/net/mac80211/util.c
===================================================================
--- backports-6.12.6.orig/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ backports-6.12.6/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -1654,7 +1654,11 @@ static void ieee80211_assign_chanctx(str
 
 	conf = rcu_dereference_protected(link->conf->chanctx_conf,
 					 lockdep_is_held(&local->hw.wiphy->mtx));
-	if (conf) {
+	/* An AP_VLAN is never added to the driver, so it must not be handed to
+	 * drv_assign_vif_chanctx(); its chanctx_conf is only a copy of the
+	 * parent AP link's pointer and is assigned when that link is.
+	 */
+	if (conf && sdata->vif.type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) {
 		ctx = container_of(conf, struct ieee80211_chanctx, conf);
 		drv_assign_vif_chanctx(local, sdata, link->conf, ctx);
 	}
